.Rproj.user
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
# Whole path, not just contents, for the same reason as /outputs below: a
# `downloads` symlink pointing at an existing copy of the inputs is the obvious
# way to avoid re-fetching 4 GB, and `downloads/*` left that symlink committable.
# It was committed once, carrying an absolute path from one machine.
/downloads
*.DS_Store
# Ignores the whole path, not just its contents: locally `outputs` is a symlink
# into personal cloud storage, and `outputs/*` alone leaves that symlink itself
# committable.
/outputs
# Legacy artefacts used as the phase 3-4 replication baseline. 404 MB, and a
# reference copy rather than a build product — do not commit.
outputs_legacy/
# Baseline artefacts as delivered, plus the archive they came from. Both exceed
# GitHub's 100 MB file limit; a `git add -A` swept them in once and the push was
# rejected by the pre-receive hook, so they are named explicitly rather than
# relied on to sit outside a pattern.
outputs*.zip
figures/*
ignore/*
ms/*
*.Rproj
*.rds
*.docx

# targets object store — local build cache, rebuilt by tar_make().
# _targets/meta/ is deliberately included in the ignore: it records absolute
# paths and per-machine build times, so sharing it across machines causes
# spurious invalidation rather than preventing it.
_targets/

# Rendered reports; rebuilt by tar_make()
*.html
*_files/

# Internal working notes, not part of the public repository
CLAUDE.md
